{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T23:01:47.892Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8a4268fe12c2a5f9fcd4da8d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-urzubi"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Starting work ignores open blockers: claim <id> --start and update --status in_progress move a blocked item into progress without a refusal or warning"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Raised by CodeRabbit on PR #1645 and verified on 2026.10.31 source in a fresh sandbox. An item created with --blocked-by <open item> is stored as status blocked, and pm update <id> --status in_progress then succeeds with no refusal or warning. pm claim <id> --start runs the same claim-then-update composition, so it behaves the same. pm validate later reports non_blocked_status_has_blocked_by for the in-progress item whose blocker is still open. pm next and claim --next --start are unaffected because ready selection already excludes items with open blockers. Starting an explicitly blocked item is a governance decision, not a claim defect, so changing only --start would make start and update disagree.\n\nDuplicate search: 'start blocked item open blocker in_progress refuse', 'non_blocked_status_has_blocked_by' — no open item. Nearest is the dependency-aware actionability decision (closed)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","dependencies","governance","lifecycle"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-31T23:01:47.892Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T23:01:47.892Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":150},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Moving an item with an open blocked_by target into the in-progress status, through update, claim --start or start-task, either refuses with a typed code naming the open blocker and the unblock or --force recovery, or warns, as governed by a declared setting; the CLI, MCP and SDK paths share one check that runs before any write, so a refused start never leaves a claim; a terminal blocker does not block; tests cover refuse, warn and terminal-blocker cases"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-33cw"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"No transport can silently move an item with an open blocker into progress; the behaviour is declared by governance settings and consistent across update and start."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-9x6k","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-31T23:01:47.892Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1643","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-10-31T23:01:47.892Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"acf3efb6d2679c95d815ce0d1449b31ba8de0d5f3998cac2b66018e7a6eeb34c","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","re