{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T16:35:50.225Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6da2f5f4d31f8f762cde8c96","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"tests_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tests/1","value":{"command":"node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/sdk/lifecycle/start-race.spec.ts","scope":"project","timeout_seconds":600,"provenance":{"author":"harness:claude-code","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:35:50.190Z","source_kind":"local_mutation","source_ref":"feat/write-time-preconditions"}}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T16:35:50.225Z"}],"before_hash":"859ed2c61b81d0009023696b5f1fa8767b2c55eade803708b9698c4f133b4269","after_hash":"5b7fbdd3193ec32e7eaa45381116bee46aaaa308a61c3f087de0a36e57ea172f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0d8068ca7c0177cf96c2b12fbfb1bcbc9f75384cb0c3e994db8ff79a4c1d3457"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T17:47:13.105Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6da2f5f4d31f8f762cde8c96","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-02T17:47:13.105Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 2+3 on PR 1654. The composed status update always re-judges under its own lock. When a blocker opens after the claim, the start releases the claim it took from no owner, and keeps the original refusal if that release fails. A deterministic race spec (start-race.spec.ts) covers it. Suggested commands render through renderPmCommand (CodeRabbit Major: stored blocker ids are now shell-quoted). Blocker kinds canonicalize (depends_on resolves instead of throwing), short aliases compare canonically and edges are cited as stored. --unset blocked_by is advertised only when no other blocked_by edge would be lost; that data-loss defect is filed as pm-4yxzvd."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T17:47:13.105Z"}],"before_hash":"5b7fbdd3193ec32e7eaa45381116bee46aaaa308a61c3f087de0a36e57ea172f","after_hash":"ee3648db005fc485c11d125fa52895d2fc73ae3c4b7883c1edb707e6563950ae","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"589e2aa39a8a9e6d92694ba19922eb607a8de90a37f191ac962b032ee7af69c0"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T18:28:28.009Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6da2f5f4d31f8f762cde8c96","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Verified in specs and against the built CLI. update/claim --start/start-task refuse with exit 4 when the claim-time check fails, writing nothing. A deterministic race spec shows a blocker opened between claim and update refuses, releases the claim from no owner (history: create, claim, update, release), keeps an earlier owner's claim with a partial-completion why, and never releases a peer's takeover. Same-call unblock+start, terminal blockers and already-in-progress items are admitted; --force and warn record their warnings. The published 2026.11.2 negative control starts the blocked item silently."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"sdk/lifecycle/start-blockers.ts owns one admission check, resolved through sdk/query/declared-blockers.ts (shared with the pm get blockers facet) and governed by governance.start_blocker_enforcement (strict default, warn, off). update --status, claim --next --start and start-task run it under the item lock of each write that would start the item. The explicit claim --start judges it before writing ownership and again at its status update. When a blocker opens between the two writes, the start releases a claim it took from no owner (fenced against a peer takeover); otherwise the refusal's why reports the partial completion. Recovery steps are shell-quoted and offered only where a single command is safe."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Moving an item with an open blocked_by target into the in-progress status, through update, claim --start or start-task, either refuses with a typed code naming the open blocker and the unblock or --force recovery, or warns, as governed by a declared setting; the CLI, MCP and SDK paths share one check that runs under the lock of each write that would start the item, so the explicit claim --start judges it before writing ownership and again before its status update; a refusal at the second check releases a claim the start took from no owner and otherwise discloses the partial completion; a terminal blocker does not block; tests cover refuse, warn, terminal-blocker and blocker-opened-between-writes cases"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T18:28:28.009Z"}],"before_hash":"ee3648db005fc485c11d125fa52895d2fc73ae3c4b7883c1edb707e6563950ae","after_hash":"0b9188e1b4ced1b3e1395573b37c7b4190d4e7f9e3f45ca68081a52e3cf80372","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Correct the closure fields to the shipped two-check composition semantics (CodeRabbit review of PR 1654)","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b940374514d5c5b2a48bf3d7b035d4fa7c50f1f527ee0821f520cc1d879bdc62"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T19:58:19.090Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6da2f5f4d31f8f762cde8c96","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.316","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-02T19:58:19.090Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 4 on PR 1654. The claim compensation is fenced under the item lock, so it never releases a peer's takeover (under warn ownership enforcement a plain release would have). Start detection uses the effective start status (resolveStartTaskInProgressStatus), including the registered in_progress fallback when the workflow names open. Warning dedupe now drops only the exact warnings the claim recorded, so a blocker found only at the status write still warns. --dep-remove is advertised only for literal blocked_by rows whose stored id survives selector normalization; legacy short-id, alias-kind and external rows get an inspection step (gap recorded on pm-4yxzvd). The refusal message no longer claims 'Nothing was written'. The acceptance criteria, resolution and actual result were corrected to the two-check composition semantics."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T19:58:19.090Z"}],"before_hash":"0b9188e1b4ced1b3e1395573b37c7b4190d4e7f9e3f45ca68081a52e3cf80372","after_hash":"5f4d0a6126c64f45769c1713aa99276e9e3f681e15bdc85756f42fbff3f96181","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"12e605a85f2c056df5743a656b8215b74a2c782bd4c319c3e0ec1629cde36aca"}
